1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,120
(This series is a fictional work created
for entertainment purposes.)

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations
agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,360
(and symbols appearing in this story
are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,160
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:10,960
(or allude to any individual,
organization or religious group)

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,400
Hey

7
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:24,400
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

8
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,160
But look at me now

9
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,840
I'm shining

10
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,640
On nights when the sky turns against me

11
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,680
When the rain falls inside my heart

12
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:35,720
I play the same old songs

13
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,920
That we used to listen to together

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,800
Your picture is still right there

15
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,560
But I'm not crying anymore

16
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,600
I used to want you so badly

17
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,000
Now I'm beginning to understand

18
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,920
That love comes and go

19
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,880
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

20
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,680
But in the end

21
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:53,520
It was just my heart learning how to move on

22
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,120
I used to say "Can't live without you"

23
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,760
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

24
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:00,960
I’m looking so good

25
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,680
Damn I don’t even try to do

26
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,240
Good without you, I’m doing fine

27
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,600
Me without you, I can manage

28
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,000
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

29
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,280
It's fine.

30
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,080
I've found it.

31
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,640
Your necklace.

32
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,560
Does it belong to your partner?

33
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,040
Thank you very much.

34
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:17,800
Please keep your promise.

35
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,760
Don't do this to others again. It's not fun.

36
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,760
I'm sorry.

37
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,800
And thank you for helping me.

38
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,480
No problem.

39
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:48,120
From now on, what's between the two of us

40
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,920
is only work, nothing but work.

41
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,720
Okay.

42
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,040
(Ms. Nichakorn, Mr. Teerach, Mr. Seungwoo)

43
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,480
(Choi Seungwoo's three rules)

44
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,960
(1. No talking about anything except work)

45
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,320
(2. Never stay within one meter)

46
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,320
(3. Never be alone...)

47
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,000
(3. Never be alone together)

48
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,240
(3. Never be alone together. Ever.)

49
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,320
One meter.

50
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,240
Sorry.

51
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,440
Dao, perfect timing.

52
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,720
I was hoping to trouble you to clean my room.

53
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,560
But I already did it, you see.

54
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:40,800
Umm...

55
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,400
Did you forget something?

56
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,280
I did, though.

57
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,280
Not yet.

58
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,440
Are you coming?

59
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,800
It's almost time for the meeting.

60
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,720
No. / No.

61
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,000
Where would you like me

62
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:34,400
to clean, Mr. Chat?

63
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:36,960
The mirror, please.

64
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,960
Yesterday I tested the color of a new product

65
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,680
and it won't come off.

66
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,159
Alright.

67
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,080
Yesterday you...

68
00:06:52,159 --> 00:06:53,720
Hello.

69
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,640
I'm almost there.

70
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,159
Yes, wait for me for a bit.

71
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,440
Oh, right!

72
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,640
I've got a whole stack of documents ready for today.

73
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,280
I have a presentation to today.

74
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,320
I'm certain

75
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,960
it'll go well today!

76
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,960
Hold on.

77
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,560
Excuse me. / Please make a room.

78
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,960
Excuse me.

79
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,440
Please make way.

80
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,560
Thank you.

81
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,600
I still can't head home yet.

82
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:44,920
I have to do some more cleaning.

83
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,040
It's exhausting.

84
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:48,920
Really. I've been at it since six this morning.

85
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,320
It's just too much, isn't it?

86
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,040
Hang in there! / We're a day laborer.

87
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,240
I'll go clean right away.

88
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,880
Are you all right?

89
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,000
I'm fine.

90
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,880
Thank you.

91
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,840
These are the two executives

92
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:07,000
who are partners of our company.

93
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,400
They'll be joining our meeting today.

94
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,400
Hello everyone.

95
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,920
I have fairly high expectations for this new product,

96
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,240
and I hope

97
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,560
your team won't let us down.

98
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,240
The product I want

99
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,000
needs a new concept that's on trend

100
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,240
and meets the needs of the new generation,

101
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,560
and we have limited time.

102
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:25,920
In that case, that's great.

103
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,480
Mr. Seungwoo should be well suited to this,

104
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,640
since the Korean market has plenty of products of this type.

105
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,400
It should be adaptable for our company.

106
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:40,400
However, our user base has diverse skin types,

107
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,400
and they also live in different climates.

108
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:44,400
We have someone at the department-head level

109
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,720
sent directly from Korea.

110
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,240
Something like this should be simple.

111
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:51,400
I'll have the team submit this presentation within two weeks.

112
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,320
You can do it right?

113
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,200
Of course.

114
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,480
This product is really good.

115
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,360
Yeah, this one is good.

116
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,160
It's pretty good.

117
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:25,400
Hey, I'm going to the canteen first, okay?

118
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,440
Sure.

119
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,960
Why do I feel like Mr. Teerach and Mr. Seungwoo

120
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:34,520
have a strange vibe between them, somehow?

121
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,960
Right? I feel the same way.

122
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,960
But if our team

123
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,120
gets both Mr. Teerach and Mr. Seungwoo to choose our work,

124
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,320
Team B will get fired even sooner.

125
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,040
So what should we do?

126
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,480
I think I have an idea.

127
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,200
I guarantee Team B won't see it coming.

128
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:13,640
Wow.

129
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:16,920
Oh, Mira.

130
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,440
I've finished our group's presentation

131
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:20,800
for the color class.

132
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,920
All that's left is sending the color-test sample images,

133
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,440
and then we can finalize the deck.

134
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,040
Okay.

135
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,760
Wow, so beautiful.

136
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,960
I really can't do this kind of thing.

137
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,680
Every time I draw, it turns out a mess.

138
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,960
It won't be a mess.

139
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,760
You just sketch it first

140
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:43,080
and then color it in the way you drew it, that's all.

141
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,400
It's so easy, want to try?

142
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:46,800
Yeah, I'll give it a try.

143
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,160
Ah, use this color.

144
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,920
Which one? Okay.

145
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,640
Pink. / Here, try it.

146
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:55,800
Use this? / Yes.

147
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,640
And then dab it on.

148
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,280
Dab it on following the lines you've drawn.

149
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,560
Draw on the eyes, right?

150
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:01,560
Yes.

151
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,760
Hey, it's pretty easy.

152
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:08,720
Right? / Hey, it's actually easy.

153
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,560
Put some lipstick.

154
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,440
Here.

155
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:14,920
See? It's pretty.

156
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,880
Hey! / I told you it was easy.

157
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,000
Nice!

158
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,280
Actually, if we imagine this

159
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,240
as an idea for a cosmetics product, it'd be good, wouldn't it?

160
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,360
People using it should find it easy to do their makeup.

161
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,440
Come to think of it,

162
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,400
that's a good idea.

163
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:39,520
Do you think Seungwoo can handle this project?

164
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,080
Well, as Ms. Nichakorn mentioned,

165
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,880
there are quite a few differences

166
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,200
between the Thai and Korean markets.

167
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,240
On top of that,

168
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:49,720
the deadline you have given him is extremely tight,

169
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,600
so there's a high risk of failing.

170
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,360
If he fails,

171
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
he'll lose his credibility as well.

172
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,280
You're quite clever, Mr. Teerach.

173
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,920
It's as if you're giving Seungwoo

174
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,280
a chance to prove himself,

175
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,440
when in reality, you're just pressuring him

176
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,880
into going back to his home country.

177
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,160
And shouldn't someone as capable as me

178
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:28,240
get a reward?

179
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,440
What kind of reward?

180
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,920
We're at work, sir.

181
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,120
Rain doesn't start work until late tonight.

182
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,680
How about we go find something fun to do in the meantime?

183
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:48,760
Ugh! We only have two weeks!

184
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,520
Who could possibly get this done in time?

185
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,800
True.

186
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,520
And there are so many trending products

187
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,400
on the market right now.

188
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:57,760
Which one should we choose,

189
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,200
and how can we make it stand out

190
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,160
and more appealing than what's already out there?

191
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,480
How about lipstick?

192
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:07,240
At the very least, it's something everyone needs,

193
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,560
whether they know how to put on makeup or not.

194
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:10,760
That's true.

195
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:13,920
Some people even own several tubes in different colors.

196
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,120
Right?

197
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,680
I was thinking the same thing as you, Ja.

198
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:21,360
We should go with lipstick since it's currently trending

199
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,960
and is also a popular makeup trend.

200
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,560
But the real question is,

201
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,080
how do we make our product stand out from other brands

202
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,800
and appeal to Gen Z?

203
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:30,800
Exactly.

204
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:32,640
Gosh!

205
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,840
Have you still not decided on a product yet?

206
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:38,000
Team A has already started working on the designs.

207
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,520
Mind your own business. Nobody asked for your opinion.

208
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:44,160
Oh, really? I was just waiting to see the losing team.

209
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,440
She's so far away. How could she hear us?

210
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,440
So nosy.

211
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,560
Why was that wretch here?

212
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:54,040
She was here to bark and stuff.

213
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,080
Don't mind her.

214
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,200
Always happening.

215
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,840
Chat. / Yes?

216
00:15:57,920 --> 00:16:01,200
Is this lipstick tester you gave me any good?

217
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,360
My niece took it to use, and she says it's great.

218
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:06,240
She says she uses it on her cheeks, eyes, and lips,

219
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,920
and she even says if it was a cream,

220
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,080
she would cover herself with it.

221
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,400
On the whole face, sis?

222
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:14,400
Yes, why? Gen Z is really into it right now.

223
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,320
Right? Gen Z loves it.

224
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,640
One stick,

225
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,200
you can apply it on your eyes, cheeks,

226
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:24,480
and the whole face.

227
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:25,960
Then what do you think

228
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:27,080
if there were a lipstick

229
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,000
that works on the eyes, cheeks, and lips,

230
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,880
with skincare benefits

231
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,720
and long-lasting wear too,

232
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:35,760
would your niece buy it?

233
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,120
Oh, if she doesn't buy it, I will!

234
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,880
It does everything like that. Right?

235
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:42,800
Right? Would you buy it?

236
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,080
Of course.

237
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,320
I think I've figured it out.

238
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,520
Oh, what are you looking at?

239
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,040
I'm scared.

240
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:58,960
Our team is going to create a multifunctional lip gloss.

241
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,440
Oh, that's a good idea!

242
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:07,079
Don't forget the tester.

243
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,520
Include me too!

244
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:10,440
Don't forget the tester. / Finish it first.

245
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,440
Oh, Nueng.

246
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:20,920
Chat, I bought some snacks for you again.

247
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,440
Are you trying to fatten me up?

248
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,079
Why are you standing here waiting? Is something up?

249
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:28,359
Why do you always know

250
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,200
what I would do?

251
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,880
If I didn't know, then I'd be crazy.

252
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,280
You see,

253
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,960
I want to help you with the trend-driven product side,

254
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:43,160
like the design. I think I can help.

255
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:45,440
But I don't think that's appropriate.

256
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:48,240
Still, we're in the same company.

257
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:53,000
But for me, if someone on the team

258
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:54,640
goes to help another team like this

259
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,480
while their own work isn't even finished,

260
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,200
I'd feel uncomfortable.

261
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:02,040
I just want to help you.

262
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,280
These three months, if you slip up...

263
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:06,480
I won't slip up.

264
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:08,280
I'm counting on you.

265
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,280
Yes.

266
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:28,400
But thank you anyway.

267
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,840
He's pretty popular.

268
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,000
(Choi Seungwoo's three rules)

269
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,080
(1. No talking about anything except work)

270
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:07,040
(3. Never be alone together. Ever.)

271
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,960
"Choi Seungwoo's three rules"

272
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:25,960
What is this?

273
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:12,760
Oh, Chat. You're home.

274
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,120
How are you? Are you tired today?

275
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,440
Would you like to eat now?

276
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,400
It's still warm. It'll be delicious.

277
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,800
